A Manufactured Home Community plan shall be developed and drawn to a scale of one inch to 100 feet and shall, at a minimum, include the following:
(a) The name of the community, the name(s) and address(es) of the owner(s) and the names and addresses of the designer or surveyor;
(b) The date, scale and north arrow;
(c) The boundaries of the perimeter of the community;
(d) The site plan of the community showing the location of streets, driveways, open areas, parking spaces, service buildings, existing buildings, water courses, easements and Manufactured Home spaces;
(e) Minimum front building setback lines for all lots;
(f) Name(s) of adjoining property owner(s);
(g) The identification and location of all gas, water, electric, telephone, cable, and sewage lines that will serve the community. Street lights, solid waste containers and surface water drainage plans shall also be shown on the plan;
(h) The current zoning designation of the tract or parcel of land;
(i) Such other information concerning the plan as may be requested by the Zoning Administrator.
16.3.1 Review and Approval of Plan. Before any permit is issued for construction of a Manufactured Home Community, the plan for the community must be submitted to the Commission to insure that the proposed Manufactured Home Community meets the requirements of this Ordinance. If the plan is approved by the Commission, the Building Inspector shall issue the necessary permits for the construction of the Manufactured Home Community.

