16.4.1 Density and Area.
(a) The maximum density within a Manufactured Home Community shall not exceed two units per acre.
(b) A Manufactured Home Community shall front on a public street, shall have a minimum frontage of 100 feet on the public street and shall contain a minimum area of five acres.
16.4.2 Setbacks.
(a) Along Public Streets. There shall be a minimum setback of fifty feet (50 ft.) along all community exterior boundaries which abut a public street;
(b) Along Rear and Side Property Lines. All community exterior boundaries not adjacent to a public street shall have a minimum setback of 25 feet;
(c) Along Community Streets. There shall be a minimum distance of 15 feet between a Manufactured Home and any abutting community street;
(d) Required Separation Between Manufactured Homes. Manufactured homes shall be separated from each other and from other buildings and structures by no less than 30 feet.
16.4.3 Lot Area. Manufactured Home lots/sites shall have a minimum lot width and area as follows:
| Single-Section Homes | Multi-Section Homes
Minimum lot width | 100 feet | 100 feet
Minimum lot area | 21,780 square feet | 21,780 square feet
16.4.4 Community Improvements.
(a) Paving, Soil and Ground Cover Requirements. Exposed ground surfaces in all parts of a Manufactured Home Community shall be paved, covered with crushed stone, or other solid material, or protected with grass or other vegetative cover that is capable of preventing soil erosion and eliminating objectionable dust.
(b) Lot/Site Drainage Requirements. The ground surface in all parts of a Manufactured Home Community shall be graded and equipped to drain all surface or storm water in a safe, efficient manner.
16.4.5 Accessory Storage Buildings for Manufactured Home Communities. One accessory storage building is allowed on an individual lot. The storage building is to be located in the rear yard of the lot and may be located no closer than ten feet to the rear lot line of the individual lot. The maximum size of the storage building shall not exceed 120 square feet in size and shall only be used for storage of personal property of the person(s) living in the Manufactured Home located on the lot.
16.4.6 Recreation Areas. Recreation areas designed for the common use of residents shall comply with the following provisions:
(a) In all Manufactured Home Communities accommodating or designed to accommodate 25 or more Manufactured Homes, there shall be one or more recreation areas;
(b) The size of such recreation areas shall be based upon a minimum of 100 square feet per each lot/site in the Manufactured Home Community;
(c) Recreation areas shall not be located near high traffic areas, retention ponds or other hazards.
16.4.7 Street System and Vehicle Parking.
(a) Manufactured Home Community Street Systems. Community street systems shall meet the following requirements:
(1) The entrance and exit streets shall be designed to provide safe and convenient access between the public street and the community interior street system;
(2) All streets shall be paved with plant mix asphalt or concrete;
(3) No local street grade shall exceed 12 percent unless the Zoning Administrator finds that due to topographic conditions, a steeper grade is necessary, in which case the street grade shall not exceed 15 percent. Street grades between 12 percent and 15 percent shall not exceed a length of 150 feet;
(4) Minimum pavement widths shall be 20 feet for two-way traffic; 14 feet for one-way traffic; and an additional minimum of seven feet shall be provided for on-street parking, if provided;
(5) Each lot or site shall be accessible from abutting streets for all essential and emergency uses by vehicular equipment, including equipment used by public agencies such as fire, police, and ambulance services;
(6) The street layout shall be designed to provide for the continuous flow of traffic, with culs-de-sac, with a minimum radius of 50 feet being permissible;
(7) Traffic control signs such as "stop," "yield," and "speed limit", shall be placed throughout the community where necessary;
(8) Each street shall have a permanent sign installed with a designated name identifying each street;
(9) All streets, parking areas, and refuse collection areas shall be maintained by the owner or manager of the Manufactured Home Community;
(10) Street lighting shall be provided throughout the community.
(b) Vehicle Parking. Off-street parking areas or on-street parking lanes shall be provided for the use of community residents and guests.
(1) A minimum area of 400 square feet of paved parking shall be provided for each lot/site;
(2) Driveways shall have a minimum width of ten feet;
(3) All off-street parking areas or spaces shall have direct access to an interior street. A driveway for a Manufactured Home lot shall not directly access an exterior street.

