This Section is established with the intention that complimentary agricultural uses should be permitted within residential districts. It is recognized that agricultural uses are in many instances complimentary to primary residential uses, and make for a more pleasant and complete living environment. This Section is not designed to permit the pursuit of agriculture primarily for commercial purposes, but does not preclude the occasional sale of agricultural commodities produced as an activity incidental to the residential use of the land.
